  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "48fcc154",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Decision threshold\n",
    "We find the optimal decision threshold using out-of-fold predictions on the training set.\n",
    "A classifier gives a probability of being a good wine. The threshold decides from which probability we label it as good (default: 0.5). We find the optimal threshold using out-of-fold predictions on the training set to avoid touching the test set\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "12eb7aedb13842eb",
   "metadata": {
    "ExecuteTime": {
     "end_time": "2026-11-01T22:59:56.060437Z",
     "start_time": "2026-11-01T22:59:55.972867Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Best threshold: 0.48\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.model_selection import cross_val_predict\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import precision_recall_curve\n",
    "\n",
    "oof_proba = cross_val_predict(best_pipeline, X_train, y_train, cv=5, method=\"predict_proba\")[:, 1]\n",
    "precision, recall, thresholds = precision_recall_curve(y_train, oof_proba)\n",
    "f1_scores = 2 * precision * recall / (precision + recall + 1e-9)\n",
    "threshold = round(float(thresholds[np.argmax(f1_scores[:-1])]), 2)\n",
    "print(f\"Best threshold: {threshold}\")"
   ]
  },
