   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6c57409b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "**Most important features.** The model relies mostly on alcohol, volatile acidity and residual sugar. This shows what the model uses, not what causes quality.\n",
    "as in adding more alcohol doesn't make a wine better, it's just a pattern found by the model.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Two limits.**\n",
    "1. The data only contains Portuguese Vinho Verde wines rated by human tasters, so the model may not work for other wines.\n",
    "2. The model is only moderately good (F1 0.81): 181 wines that are not good were called good so that means the merchant would still waste time on some bad wines.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Ethical risks.**\n",
    "The model’s definition of ‘good’ is based on scores from one tasting panel. A small producer whose style differs from what that panel prefers could be unfairly penalized. The model gives a probability but no explanation of which features caused the rejection."
   ]
  }
